 ## 10\. Functional Requirements

 ### FR-01: User Registration

 The system shall allow new students to create an account.

 ### FR-02: User Login

 The system shall authenticate registered users.

 ### FR-03: AI Chat

 The system shall allow students to submit educational questions and receive AI-generated responses.

 ### FR-04: Concept Explanation

 The system shall provide explanations based on the requested subject and difficulty level.

 ### FR-05: Quiz Generation

 The system shall generate questions based on a selected topic.

 ### FR-06: Quiz Evaluation

 The system shall evaluate submitted answers and calculate a score.

 ### FR-07: Summarization

 The system shall generate concise summaries from valid study content.

 ### FR-08: Learning History

 The system shall store relevant learning activities for later reference.

 ### FR-09: Progress Tracking

 The system shall display basic learning activity and quiz-performance information.

 ### FR-10: Error Handling

 The system shall display appropriate messages when requests fail or invalid input is provided.

 ## 11\. Non-Functional Requirements

 ### Performance

 The application should respond efficiently under normal usage conditions.

 ### Usability

 The interface should be simple enough for students to navigate without extensive instructions.

 ### Security

 User credentials and API credentials must be protected.

 ### Reliability

 The system should handle API, network, and database failures gracefully.

 ### Scalability

 The architecture should allow additional subjects, users, and features to be added later.

 ### Maintainability

 The application should use modular frontend, backend, and service components.

